/code-review high 2026-10-08-release-tasks-bump (round 3)

1. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:177 — The release target is computed from the last tag plus a level, never from the manifest. A manifest hand-bumped more than one step ahead of its tag is silently rewritten to a lower version. Tag stackgen-v3.0.0, plugin.json 3.4.0, no key: level_implied MINOR, release_target 3.1.0, plugin.json overwritten with 3.1.0; dry-run shows only '-> 3.1.0'. Same in p:i:release:119 and p:site:release:191 (site 1.1.50 tagged, manifest 1.1.55, releases 1.1.51). Tests cover only one step ahead. (open gap G1)
2. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:47 — The pr-model guard reads MERGE_MODEL_MAIN first, but code:merge:main reads only MERGE_MODEL (_scripts/merge:150), so guard and merge can disagree: MERGE_MODEL_MAIN=direct with a stale MERGE_MODEL=pr passes the guard, the merge opens a PR without merging, and the tags name the old main. Same guard in the three sibling tasks.
3. .config/mise/tasks/p/site/release:109 — On the standalone --tag-only path the local tag is created before require_gh runs (git tag -a at :99, require_gh after). The next run fails with 'site-vX already exists'. require_gh at :166 covers only full mode. p:i:release:36-46 checks gh before any tag for --tag-only.
4. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:155 — Resume instructions are wrong when code:merge:main stops on a merge conflict: the tree is left mid-merge on main, ON_MAIN is false, so the resume says 'Resume from develop with: mise run code:merge:main', which is refused from main; nothing mentions git merge --abort; the EXIT trap's git switch -q develop also fails on the conflicted tree.
5. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:165 — With no prior tag, the level calculation is skipped and the manifest released as it stands; a recorded level is shown but never applied and the key cleared. A plugin with no tag and no record always counts as 'to release', so p:release would plan a bump and merge for it on every run.
6. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:100 — The gates run once on develop before the bump; the tag steps on main skip them through RELEASE_GATES_DONE=1, so the merge commit that gets tagged is never gated if main differs from develop.
7. .config/mise/tasks/_scripts/local:150 — releases_level reads the first matching key, but releases_raise rewrites every matching line and releases_clear deletes every matching line; a duplicated key behaves inconsistently.
8. .config/mise/tasks/p/i/release:112 — The last-tag/recorded/implied/target computation and the gh checks and tag_step bodies are copy-pasted across the three tasks with slightly different control flow; one shared function in _scripts/local would remove the drift.
9. .github/workflows/deps-update.yml:80 — The monthly job merges all of develop into main to publish a dependency refresh even when other release levels or untagged plugin manifests are pending; the marketplace manifest on main then names refs with no tags and plugins.yml stays red on main until a person runs p:release.
